    "created_at": "2026-06-23T21:58:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-24T18:34:05Z",
    "body": "This is not a fully formed thought but I dont believe its actually necessary to style the button or to provide that option, as with code its possible to swap out GIFs or show a particular frame? I believe this is in instance, similar to controls like a color picker or video element, the native functionality would provide a consistent as possible experience. The real fundamental goal here in my mind is to prevent the bad qualities of undesired GIFs and lack of control over initiating or stopping them from a sensible defaults perspective. The customization styling can occur without any blocker to my mind- the real goal is to insert the sensible default option with the attribute. Just my view.",
