    "created_at": "2026-06-25T03:40:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-25T18:51:33Z",
    "body": "@o-t-w I wanted to offer an alternative to the idea that opening images at full screen would lead to a bad user experience. It could be made to open the image at its max-width, natural size, in the center of the screen for example. \n\nIf the image had a larger resolution size capable than was visible on the page, it would be an opportunity to enhance the image with a native controls viewer, which could seem to be a potential benefit to people with some disabilities or preferences who simply may want to see things bigger to understand them.\n\nConsidered in this way, its got web design features of a lightbox pattern or gallery-like pattern. Except it would be baked into the living standard, with some degree of ubiquity and sustainability arguably also as well.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
